{"id":"resp_94bb9a98ac3e03d2","created_at":1795618192,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_a250e280eb527f52","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to revise SHACL to address admissions scope error: target classes selection beyond declared population. The admission declares focus_set owner_class = iceClassDesignParameterSet. So SHACL should target that class, not others. Currently shape nltl:IceClassDesignParameterSetShape targets class nltl:iceClassDesignParameterSet (different prefix). Need to use correct IRI from contract: target_owner is \"iceClassDesignParameterSet\". The IRI in ontology is https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClassDesignParameterSet. So adjust sh:targetClass to that IRI. Also need to adjust property paths maybe referencing designIceLoadHeight and levelIceThickness which are defined with that class.\n\nThus modify shape IRI maybe rename to proper IRI like :IceClassDesignParameterSetShape but sh:targetClass to https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClassDesignParameterSet.\n\nKeep other constraints unchanged.\n\nAlso address unresolved_context: target cannot be bound to explicit model owner line 10 column 20. That's same issue. So fix that.\n\nWe must not delete constraints.\n\nReturn whole SHACL with updated target.\n\nAlso ensure prefixes used: nltl prefix currently points to https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#. The class is nltl:iceClassDesignParameterSet. That's same as target_owner? contract says target_owner = \"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClassDesignParameterSet\". So using nltl:iceClassDesignParameterSet is fine. But the earlier shape uses nltl:IceClassDesignParameterSetShape (capital I) naming is fine.\n\nCurrent targetClass line is \"sh:targetClass nltl:iceClassDesignParameterSet ;\". That matches target. Wait, earlier we see they used \"sh:targetClass nltl:iceClassDesignParameterSet ;\". Indeed line 10. So why unresolved? maybe case sensitivity? In schema, class IRI is exactly that. The issue may be they used s:IceClassDesignParameterSetShape vs nltl:IceClassDesignParameterSetShape as shape name, but target is fine. However the error message says other target classes select beyond declared population. Maybe other shapes? The quantity shape targets qudt:QuantityValue which is outside declared population. That's fine because it's a utility shape not bound to owner. But maybe they consider it as target. Admission only allows target class iceClassDesignParameterSet; other shapes with targetClass cause error. So need to remove sh:targetClass from QuantityValue shape, maybe use sh:targetObjectsOf? Instead we can make that shape a property shape without targetClass. To keep validation of QuantityValue used as node, we could use sh:targetNode? It expects node maybe in data. But we want to apply shape to nodes used in property values. We can instead not set targetClass for QuantityValue shape; just define it as a node shape to be used via sh:node. This will not be considered a target class outside scope. So remove sh:targetClass from _:QuantityValueShape.\n\nThus modify that section: remove sh:targetClass qudt:QuantityValue; leaving just a shape definition (maybe blank node) that can be used.\n\nEverything else unchanged.\n\nReturn SHACL.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_9861d014fe946729","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n\n# Shape that validates a QUDT QuantityValue (used via sh:node, not a target class)\n_:QuantityValueShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\n        sh:hasValue unit:M ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n    ] .\n\n# Shape for Ice Class Design Parameter Set – the only admitted target class\nnltl:IceClassDesignParameterSetShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:iceClassDesignParameterSet ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:levelIceThickness ;\n        sh:node _:QuantityValueShape ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:description \"Level ice thickness (hi) for the ice class.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:designIceLoadHeight ;\n        sh:node _:QuantityValueShape ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:description \"Design ice load height (h) for the ice class.\" ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":72213,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":320,"cache_write_tokens":71888,"input_tokens_per_turn":[72213],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[320]},"output_tokens":1067,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":679,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1067],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":73280},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}